 * SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
 *
 * I2C gather-write topology: parent and I2C okay, everything else disabled.
 *
 * GPIO and SPI stay disabled. This image touches nothing but the I2C bus, and
 * an enabled SPI controller would additionally park every cs-gpios pin as an
 * inactive output at init, which this test has no reason to provoke.
 *
 * No target device node is declared. The test drives raw i2c_* calls
 * deliberately: the subject is the controller's message-group handling, and
 * binding a sensor driver would hide the very message shapes being exercised.
 * The target address and register live in src/main.c.
 *
 * No serial-number is declared either, matching samples/i2c_bridge. That is
 * safe only when exactly one board is attached; see "Selecting a specific
 * board" in zephyr/README.md if you have several. Only GPIO and SPI children
 * require the parent to name a serial, because they actuate physical pins.
 */

&pdg0 {
	status = "okay";
};

&pdg_i2c0 {
	status = "okay";
};
